// Negative case for plan-v5 R1b, the version pin that selects.
//
// A pin now picks which version of a module script to build against, which means a pin naming a
// version the asset does not have must be an error rather than a silently ignored decoration. The
// old contract -- "the pin records what this was written against and the build refuses to use a
// different one" -- could not tell those apart, because it never selected anything.
//
// The message lists the versions the asset does offer, because "5.0 is not available" is only
// actionable next to "1.0, 2.0 are".
//
// EXPECT DFX3009
System(Name="Corpus/NS_UnknownModuleVersion", Root="Plugin.DreamFX")
{
    Emitter Sparks
    {
        ParticleUpdate = {
            ScaleColor@99.7(ScaleAlpha = 0.5);
        }
    }
}
